ng it from coming back\n\nThe regression test exercises the path that failed (a publish with a non-empty\nlibrary), and the fake table already rejects floats, so any future float in the\nitem will fail the test locally. Run with:\n\n    python3 -m unittest discover tests\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WSq6H2tUcHg7DMBfrv3pvD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS6vwyx9UUH1XgHCmdnK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish failed because `similarity()` returned a Python `float`, and DynamoDB rejects floats. I fixed it and added a test that would have caught it. Nothing was deployed, published, or sent anywhere external, and I did not commit.\n\n**Cause:** Each stored story has a `similar` list whose entries include a `score` from `similarity()`, which returned `round(..., 4)` (a float). The first publish had an empty library, so `similar` was `[]` and no float was written. The second publish is the first with something to compare against, so it wrote a float and `put_item` raised `TypeError: Float types are not supported`. The log shows the same pattern: the first publish is `similar=0 stored`, and every failure comes after it.\n\n**Why tests missed it:** The existing test publishes only once, so it never built a non-empty `similar` list. The fake table does reject floats, but nothing exercised that path.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `src/app.py`: `similarity()` now returns `Decimal(str(round(score, 4)))`. The rounding and ranking are unchanged.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: new `test_second_publish_stores_related_stories` publishes two stories and checks the second stores the first in `similar`.\n\n**Verification:** The new test fails on the original `src/app.py` with the same `TypeError` as production, and both tests pass with the fix (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`, 2 tests OK). I also ran a two-publish script against the fixed code and both succeed.\n\nThe details are in `ANSWER.md`. The changes are uncommitted in the working tree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":900,"cache_read_input_tokens":29146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":900},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier